{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791880244,"nonce":"IDlzFGlIjOht/vr9lb6wpamQC5A=","title":"Select and Accordion ignore declarative HXX child fragments","message":"On local HEAD acc3b94, Select collects only directly authored Option/Optgroup children; Accordion collects only directly authored AccordionItem children. Equivalent \u003cfor\u003e and \u003cif\u003e children are visible in the UI tree but are ignored by their parent control. A clip picker silently resets a valid selection to its first directly authored option; a conditional accordion section remains closed and Enter cannot open it.\n\nFocused reproducer: /Users/amaterasu/Vibranium/chimpmonk/repro/ashui_component_fragments/Repro.hx. Compile with the editor/editor.hxml macro/classpaths, -cp repro/ashui_component_fragments -main Repro -hl editor/bin/component-fragments.hl, then run ash --preset application editor/bin/component-fragments.hl.\n\nActual output: directSelect=walk, repeatedSelect=empty, conditionalSelect=empty; directAccordion=open, conditionalAccordionBefore=closed, conditionalAccordionAfterEnter=closed. Expected equivalent selections and working conditional accordion binding/navigation. ChimpMonk currently supplies concrete arrays of authored children as a narrow compatibility measure. See existing Command declarative-children issue 6a88875. Support fragment traversal/registration and disposal without losing owner lifetimes, option selection or accordion keyboard order.","files":null}]}